:: hospital.sasha.first-meeting -> @exit
  @place-key hospital
  @auto enter-place
  @priority 500
  @when (hospital.needsTreatment or flags.hospital.awaiting_sasha_introduction) and hospital.sashaOnDuty and not npc.sasha.met

  @onenter
    @effect relationship sasha.interest 1
    @effect unset flags.hospital.awaiting_sasha_introduction
  @endonenter

  A doctor looks up from your chart and comes over to check on you. {{npc.sasha.subject | cap}} lab coat is pressed and clean. Looking up you meet {{npc.sasha.object}} eyes through {{npc.sasha.dependent}} square glasses.
  "I'm Dr. Sasha Volkov," the doctor says, looking you up and down. "You're welcome here anytime. Let's see what needs treating."

  @next "Thank {{npc.sasha.object}}" -> @exit

:: hospital.sasha.follow-up -> @exit
  @place-key hospital
  @auto enter-place
  @priority 400
  @when hospital.sashaOnDuty and npc.sasha.met and flags.hospital.treatment_received and not flags.hospital.sasha_followup_done

  @onenter
    @effect set flags.hospital.sasha_followup_done
    @effect relationship sasha.interest 1
  @endonenter

  Dr. Volkov recognises you while crossing the waiting area. "I saw you were treated here. How have you been feeling since?"

  @if hospital.needsTreatment
    You mention the injury that brought you back. {{npc.sasha.dependent | cap}} expression turns attentive. "Then let's take a fresh look. Don't try to push through something that isn't improving."
  @else
    You tell {{npc.sasha.object}} you're moving more comfortably now. "Good," Sasha says. "It's nice to see someone come back with better news."
  @endif

  @next "Thank {{npc.sasha.object}}" -> @exit

:: hospital.sasha.injury-advice -> @exit
  @place-key hospital
  @offer npc sasha
  @label "Ask Dr. Volkov about your injuries"
  @when hospital.sashaOnDuty and npc.sasha.met and hospital.needsTreatment

  Sasha checks your chart, then asks you to describe what hurts and what has stopped working normally.

  @if hospital.hasUnrecoverableInjury
    "This injury is too severe to mend on its own," Sasha tells you. "Please let us treat it here instead of waiting for it to improve."
  @else
    "It should improve gradually with time," Sasha says. "If you want it dealt with now, we can treat it here."
  @endif

  @next "Thank {{npc.sasha.object}}" -> @exit

:: hospital.sasha.about-work -> @exit
  @place-key hospital
  @offer npc sasha
  @label "Ask Sasha about work"
  @when hospital.sashaOnDuty and npc.sasha.met and not flags.hospital.sasha_work_chat_done

  @onenter
    @effect set flags.hospital.sasha_work_chat_done
    @effect relationship sasha.interest 1
  @endonenter

  During a quiet moment at the desk, you ask Sasha what keeps {{npc.sasha.object}} working these long shifts.

  "The work can be exhausting," Sasha admits. "But sometimes someone walks out of here who couldn't walk in. I try to remember those days."

  A call from the corridor draws {{npc.sasha.dependent}} attention. Before leaving, Sasha gives you a small smile. "Ask me again when it isn't so busy."

  @next "Let {{npc.sasha.object}} get back to work" -> @exit

:: place.hospital
  @hub hospital
  @choices "Things to do"

  A row of seats faces the reception desk. Staff move between the waiting area and the treatment rooms, keeping the hospital open around the clock.
